12
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Into the Abyss (subtitled A Tale of Death, a Tale of Life) is a 2011
documentary film written and directed by Werner Herzog.

13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
It is about capital punishment, and focuses on a triple homicide
that occurred in Montgomery County, Texas, in 2001.

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
In the film, Herzog interviews the two young men convicted of the crime, Michael Perry (who received a death sentence) and Jason Burkett (who was given a life
sentence), as well as family members and acquaintances of the victims and criminals, and individuals who have taken part in executions in Texas.

15
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
The primary focus of the film is not the details of the case or the question of Michael and Jason's guilt or innocence, and,
although Herzog's voice can be heard as he conducts the interviews, there is a minimal amount of narration.

16
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
He never appears onscreen, unlike in many of his films.

17
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
The film was first screened on September 3, 2011, at the Telluride Film Festival, and had its
official world premiere on September 8 at the Toronto International Film Festival.

18
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
After strong festival showings and a surge of interest in the issue of capital punishment in the United States, Herzog
requested that the film be rushed into general theatrical release, which occurred on November 11, 2011.

19
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:06,000
The film explores themes of death penalty, texas, death
row, capital punishment, death row inmate.

20
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
The tone is thought_provoking.
